export const TERMS_OF_SERVICE = "# BChat Terms of Service\n\n**Effective date:** September 28, 2026\n\nWelcome to BChat. These Terms of Service (\"Terms\") are an agreement between you and the BChat team (\"BChat,\" \"we,\" \"us\"), a group of student developers who build and run the BChat app. By creating an account or using BChat, you agree to these Terms. If you don't agree, don't use the app.\n\n**BChat is an independent student project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA) or the Regents of the University of California.** \"UCLA\" is used only to describe who the app is for.\n\n## 1. Who can use BChat\n\nTo use BChat, you must:\n\n- be a current UCLA student with a valid UCLA email address (`@ucla.edu` or `@g.ucla.edu`);\n- be at least 13 years old; and\n- if you are under 18, have permission from a parent or legal guardian to use BChat and agree to these Terms.\n\nYou may not use BChat if we have previously banned you.\n\n## 2. Your account\n\nYou sign in with your UCLA Google account. You are responsible for everything that happens under your account, so keep your device and Google account secure. Don't share your account, create accounts for other people, or impersonate anyone.\n\n## 3. How BChat works\n\nWhen you add your courses, BChat automatically adds you to a group chat for each class. **Everything you post in a chat — messages, photos, videos, reactions, and your display name and profile picture — is visible to every member of that chat.** Treat class chats like a room full of classmates, not a private conversation.\n\n## 4. Zero tolerance for objectionable content and abusive users\n\nBChat has **zero tolerance** for objectionable content and abusive behavior. You agree not to post, send, or share anything that:\n\n- harasses, bullies, threatens, stalks, or intimidates anyone;\n- is hateful or discriminatory based on race, ethnicity, national origin, religion, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic;\n- is sexually explicit, pornographic, or sexualizes anyone, or involves minors in any sexual way;\n- promotes violence, self-harm, or illegal activity;\n- shares someone else's private information (such as their address, phone number, or photos) without permission;\n- is spam, scams, advertising, or repetitive unwanted messages;\n- infringes someone else's copyright, trademark, or other rights (for example, posting copyrighted course materials you don't have the right to share); or\n- impersonates another person or misrepresents your affiliation with anyone.\n\nYou also agree not to:\n\n- use BChat to violate the UCLA Student Conduct Code or academic integrity rules, including sharing exam or quiz answers during an assessment;\n- use bots, scripts, or automated tools to access or post to BChat;\n- try to access other users' accounts or chats you aren't a member of; or\n- interfere with, overload, reverse-engineer, or probe the security of the app or its servers.\n\n## 5. Reporting and blocking\n\nIf you see content or a user that breaks these Terms, report it using the report option in the app. You can also block users so you no longer see their messages.\n\nWe review reports and **act on objectionable content within 24 hours**. Depending on what happened, we may remove the content, warn the user, restrict their account, or permanently ban them. Anyone who posts objectionable content may be removed from BChat immediately and without warning.\n\n## 6. Your content\n\nYou own the messages, photos, and videos you post (\"Your Content\"). By posting it, you give BChat a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to store, display, and deliver Your Content to the members of the chats you post it in, only as needed to run the app.\n\nYou are responsible for Your Content and confirm that you have the right to share it. We may remove any content at any time if we believe it violates these Terms or could harm other users.\n\n## 7. Notifications\n\nIf you allow them, BChat sends push notifications about new messages and replies. You can change notification settings in the app or turn them off in your device settings.\n\n## 8. Ending your account\n\nYou can stop using BChat at any time and delete your account from the app's Settings. Deleting your account removes your profile and personal information. For more about what happens to your data, see our Privacy Policy.\n\nWe may suspend or terminate your account at any time if you break these Terms, if required by law, or to protect other users or the app.\n\n## 9. Privacy\n\nOur Privacy Policy explains what information we collect and how we use it. By using BChat, you agree to that Privacy Policy.\n\n## 10. Changes to BChat and these Terms\n\nBChat is a student project and may change, pause, or shut down at any time. We may update these Terms from time to time. If we make significant changes, we will let you know in the app. If you keep using BChat after the changes take effect, you accept the updated Terms.\n\n## 11. Disclaimers\n\nBChat is provided **\"as is\" and \"as available,\"** without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We don't guarantee that the app will always be available, secure, or error-free, or that messages will always be delivered.\n\nWe don't check what users post before it appears, and we aren't responsible for content posted by other users. Information shared by classmates (for example, about assignments or exams) may be wrong; always rely on your instructor and official course materials.\n\n## 12. Limitation of liability\n\nTo the fullest extent allowed by law, BChat and its team members will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data, arising from your use of the app. Our total liability for any claim related to BChat will not exceed $50 USD.\n\nSome jurisdictions don't allow certain limitations, so some of the above may not apply to you.\n\n## 13. Apple App Store\n\nIf you downloaded BChat from the Apple App Store:\n\n- These Terms are between you and BChat, not Apple. Apple is not responsible for the app or its content.\n- Apple has no obligation to provide maintenance or support for the app.\n- If the app fails to meet any applicable warranty, you may notify Apple, and Apple may refund the purchase price (if any). Apple has no other warranty obligation for the app.\n- Apple is not responsible for addressing any claims relating to the app, including product liability claims, claims that the app fails to meet legal or regulatory requirements, or consumer protection claims.\n- If a third party claims the app infringes their intellectual property, BChat, not Apple, is responsible for handling that claim.\n- You confirm that you are not located in a country subject to a U.S. government embargo and are not on any U.S. government list of prohibited or restricted parties.\n- You must also follow any applicable third-party terms (such as your wireless carrier's) when using the app.\n- Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them against you.\n\n## 14. Governing law\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to its conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute will be handled in the state or federal courts located in Los Angeles County, California.\n\n## 15. Contact us\n\nQuestions or concerns about these Terms? Email us at **bchatdevx@gmail.com**.\n";

export const PRIVACY_POLICY = "# BChat Privacy Policy\n\n**Effective date:** September 28, 2026\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains what information BChat (\"BChat,\" \"we,\" \"us\") collects, how we use it, who we share it with, and the choices you have. BChat is run by a team of student developers and is an independent project, **not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by UCLA**.\n\nThe short version: we collect what we need to run class group chats, we don't sell your data, we don't show ads, and we don't track you across other apps or websites.\n\n## 1. Information we collect\n\n### Information from your Google sign-in\n\nWhen you sign in with your UCLA Google account, Google shares the following with us:\n\n- your UCLA email address;\n- your name;\n- your Google profile picture (if you have one); and\n- a Google account ID that lets us recognize you next time you sign in.\n\nWe do not receive your Google password, and we don't access your Gmail, Drive, or any other Google data.\n\nFrom your email address, we create a username (the part before the `@`).\n\n### Information you give us\n\n- **Profile details:** your display name, profile picture, class year, major, and what you want from BChat (from the sign-up questions). Year, major, and goal are optional.\n- **Courses:** the UCLA courses you add, which determine the class chats you join.\n- **Messages and media:** the messages, photos, videos, replies, and emoji reactions you post, and when you posted, edited, or deleted them.\n- **Reports:** if you report a user or message, the reason and any details you provide.\n- **Feedback:** anything you send through the in-app feedback form.\n\n### Information collected automatically\n\n- **Push notification token:** if you allow notifications, your device gives us a token so we can send notifications to it.\n- **Notification settings and theme choice:** your preferences for notifications and light/dark mode.\n- **Technical information:** like any internet service, our servers receive your IP address and basic request information when the app connects to them. We use your IP address briefly to prevent abuse (for example, limiting how fast requests can be made). Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs for a limited time.\n\nWe **do not** collect your precise location, contacts, browsing history, or advertising identifiers, and we don't use third-party analytics or advertising tools.\n\n## 2. How we use your information\n\nWe use your information to:\n\n- verify that you are a UCLA student and sign you in;\n- add you to the right class chats and show your messages to your classmates;\n- deliver messages, media, and push notifications;\n- show your name and profile picture next to your messages;\n- review reports, enforce our Terms of Service, and keep BChat safe (including warning or banning users);\n- prevent spam, abuse, and security problems;\n- respond to your feedback and support requests; and\n- fix bugs and improve the app.\n\n## 3. What other users can see\n\n- **Members of your class chats** can see your display name, profile picture, and everything you post in those chats (messages, photos, videos, replies, and reactions).\n- Your email address, Google account ID, class year, major, and goal are **not** shown to other users.\n\nMessages are not end-to-end encrypted. Members of the BChat team who run the app can access messages and account information when needed to operate the app, investigate reports, or enforce our Terms.\n\n## 4. Who we share information with\n\nWe **do not sell** your personal information and **do not share it for advertising**.\n\nWe share information only with service providers that help us run BChat, and only as needed for them to provide their service:\n\n| Provider | What they do | Information involved |\n|---|---|---|\n| Google | Sign-in | Your UCLA Google account details during sign-in |\n| MongoDB Atlas | Database hosting | Account information, messages, courses, reports, and feedback |\n| Cloudinary | Image and media hosting | Profile pictures and media you upload |\n| Expo, Apple, and Google push services | Push notifications | Your push token and notification content |\n| Our server hosting provider | Runs the BChat server | Data passing through our servers, IP addresses, and server logs |\n\nWe may also disclose information if required by law (for example, a valid subpoena or court order), or if we believe in good faith it's necessary to protect the safety of any person or to prevent fraud or abuse.\n\nIf BChat's ownership changes (for example, the project is handed off to a new student team), your information may be transferred as part of that change, and this Privacy Policy will continue to apply.\n\n## 5. How long we keep information\n\n- **Account information** is kept while your account is active.\n- **Messages and media** are kept until you delete them or delete your account. When you delete a message, its text and media are removed; a placeholder showing that a message was deleted may remain in the chat.\n- **Reports** are kept for up to 12 months after they are resolved, so we can handle repeat abuse.\n- **Feedback** is kept for as long as it's useful for improving the app.\n- If your account is **banned**, we may keep your email address and Google account ID to prevent you from creating a new account.\n\n## 6. Deleting your account and your choices\n\n- **Delete your account:** you can delete your account from Settings in the app. This deletes your profile, email address, Google account ID, courses, push token, and the messages and media you posted. Information is removed from our active systems within 30 days, except where we need to keep it as described in Section 5 or by law.\n- **Edit your profile:** you can change your display name, profile picture, and courses in the app.\n- **Delete messages:** you can delete your own messages at any time.\n- **Notifications:** you can turn notifications off in the app's Settings or in your device settings.\n- **Other requests:** to ask what information we have about you or to request a correction or deletion, email **bchatdevx@gmail.com**. We may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.\n\n## 7. Security\n\nWe use reasonable measures to protect your information, including sending data over encrypted (HTTPS) connections and limiting who on the team can access the database. No system is perfectly secure, so we can't guarantee the security of your information. If you think your account has been compromised, contact us right away.\n\n## 8. Children\n\nBChat is for UCLA students and is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has created an account, contact us and we will delete it.\n\n## 9. California residents\n\nIf you are a California resident, you have the right to know what personal information we collect, to request deletion of it, to correct it, and to not be discriminated against for exercising these rights. We do not sell or share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising. To make a request, email **bchatdevx@gmail.com**.\n\n## 10. Changes to this policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make significant changes, we will let you know in the app. The \"Effective date\" at the top shows when it was last updated.\n\n## 11. Contact us\n\nQuestions about this Privacy Policy or your information? Email **bchatdevx@gmail.com**.\n";

